  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: pp-react-worldready (npm)",
  "details": "The package pp-react-worldready@1.0.0 runs a preinstall hook (node vishu.js) that silently collects host metadata at install time. It fetches the machine's public IP from api[.]ipify[.]org, then exfiltrates the IP and CI/CD environment variables (GITHUB_ACTIONS, GITHUB_WORKFLOW, GITHUB_RUN_ID, GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER, GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT) to webhook[.]site/1b840cbf-f1a4-4d79-bf11-f1ef62949110 via HTTP GET. It also performs a DNS lookup to ping-\u003chostname\u003e.your-collab-domain[.]oastify[.]com as an out-of-band exfiltration channel. The package contains no React code and serves no legitimate purpose.",
